    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on exploiting weak opposing starters, led by our strongest play, **Taylor Ward** (71.46), who benefits from a favorable 4.89 xERA matchup and significant park factors. **Gleyber Torres** (67.52) also anchors the roster today; he draws a prime platoon edge against a lefty, and his position at the top of the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.72) and **Gavin Sheets** (63.36) round out our top-tier targets, both enjoying high-efficiency matchups against Lowder and Gibson respectively, where high xERA metrics should translate to solid counting stats. While **Jonathan Aranda** (63.76) faces a tougher arm in Soriano, his dynamic platoon advantage and promotion to the two-hole make him a high-floor start.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Matt Chapman** (44.81) on the bench. While his underlying metrics against Brown were decent, he failed to crack the top nine, as the lineup depth provided by players like **Gavin Sheets** and **Geraldo Perdomo** offered better efficiency given the current SP skill sets. **Luis Arraez** (47.23) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.94) remain in the lineup despite lower scores because their specific skill sets\u2014particularly in the AVG category\u2014are vital for our daily balance, even against the tough 3.33 xERA of Brown. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (57.43) matchup closely; facing an elite arm like Skubal is a risk, but his BvP history and the protection of hitting second keep him in the mix. Conversely, we\u2019ve benched **Bryson Stott** (38.42) and **Drew Gilbert** (37.03) as they fell below our 40-point efficiency floor, and we continue to navigate the absence of **Cal Raleigh** while he remains on the IL. With SB being our scarcest category, we are prioritizing players who can capitalize on high-walk, high-OBP environments to provide opportunistic base-stealing lanes today.",
